{"parentUuid":"89c7c392-8812-44e5-b81a-8bde68793091","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyPZ7sWQvKDMfKTW2gHX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The rung ladder already separates \"told\" (inferential) from \"checked and enforced\" (deterministic), so I'll give a single rule both forms, with promotion requiring the deterministic form and demotion keeping it while stopping its run. I'm adding this as its own phase after the scopes in the plan now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3415,"cache_read_input_tokens":705492,"output_tokens":3229,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1787},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3415,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3229,"cache_read_input_tokens":705492,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3415},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ea9da6c7-6adc-4c95-b38e-fd29e0d97dc2","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyPZ7EZSbX2dxp3Buk3T","type":"assistant","uuid":"6326e2e5-ad78-4f67-b7cb-d73d80710ed6","timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:59:16.137Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"6326e2e5-ad78-4f67-b7cb-d73d80710ed6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyPZ7sWQvKDMfKTW2gHX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qpe6o8pbtqvmeARBRKK4px","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Open questions')\nhead='''# Bastion plan: rules at three scopes, in two forms\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nA constraint or a grant is one item, and three scopes turn it on or off:\nall workflows, one workflow, and one step. The most specific setting wins,\nso a rule can be on for all workflows, off for one workflow, and on again\nat one of its steps. A rule also has two forms. An agent judges a told rule\nor a reviewer's verdict; code judges a word match, a hook, or a review\ncheck. Promoting a rule moves it from the first form to the second. The\ncost is reading: each row now says where its setting comes from.\n\nThe capabilities plan (C1 to C4) is done, and git history holds it.\nDecisions are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 and D55.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit\nbefore the next one starts.\n\n### G1. Scopes in the core and the server (D54)\n\n- A constraint's and a grant's scope list holds settings: `*` for all\n  workflows, `bug-fix` for one workflow, `bug-fix/build` for one step, and\n  `!` before any of them for off.\n- At a step, its own setting wins, then its workflow's, then the all\n  workflows setting. A list with no `*` keeps today's meaning: on at every\n  step when it names no step to turn on, and on only where it says\n  otherwise.\n- A grant is an item for one kind and one function, with its rung. A\n  step's own grants no longer replace its kind's: a step turns items on or\n  off. The gate folds the few step grants from before into items once.\n- `PUT /scopes` sets an item's setting at a scope: on, off, or inherit.\n\n### G2. Levels on the Workflows page\n\n- A level bar: All workflows › the workflow › the step. Picking a step on\n  the canvas opens its level, and the canvas background opens the\n  workflow's.\n- Each level shows the same Rules view: the charter, the harness and the\n  factory. Each item has an Inherit | On | Off switch, says what it\n  inherits, and keeps its rung switch.\n- The Add bar adds an item on at the level it is on.\n\n### G3. One rule, two forms (D55)\n\n- A constraint shows how it is judged: by an agent (told, or a reviewer)\n  or by code (a word match, a hook, or a review check).\n- Promoting a told rule asks for its deterministic form: the words a call\n  holds, or a hook command. Demoting keeps that form and stops running it.\n- A grant's rung stays ask or allowed.\n\n'''\ns=head+s[i:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| D53 |'); j=s.index('\\n',i)+1\ns=s[:j]+'''| D54 | A constraint or a grant is one item that three scopes turn on or off: all workflows (`*`), one workflow, and one step, each with `!` for off. The most specific setting wins. A list with no `*` means every step when it turns no step on, and only the steps it names otherwise. A grant is an item for one kind and one function; a step turns items on or off rather than replacing its kind's grants, which replaces D48's \"take the place of\". A rung belongs to the item, not to a scope. |\n| D55 | A constraint is judged by an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or by code (a word match, a hook, a review check). Promoting a told rule gives it a deterministic form; demoting keeps the form and stops running it. |\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py PLAN.md 2>&1 | head -5","description":"Write the scopes plan and D54, D55"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_seque