{"parentUuid":"2f3822ae-81c6-4166-b480-c13fb554428b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgybAPJwpXLrqFbNYwE4p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wow1AyMXZeejD4b6jVhEdw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo fmt --all -- --check && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''- A grant's rung stays ask or allowed.\n'''\nnew='''- A grant's rung stays ask or allowed.\n- \"Form\" on a rule edits that form at any rung.\n\nDone 2026-11-12. Live, at All workflows a told test rule showed \"agent\njudges it\". Enforced opened its form, which asked for calls to match or a\nhook; with `./.agents/hooks/lint.sh` it saved as an enforced hook, \"code\njudges it\". Told then kept the hook and stopped it running. The audit kept\nthe form, both promotions, and both demotions.\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add PLAN.md crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules/constraints.rs crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules/mod.rs crates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs crates/bastion-server/src/api/govern.rs crates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs crates/bastion-server/src/http.rs && git commit -q -m \"G3: one rule, two forms (D55)\n\nEach constraint says who judges it: an agent, for a told rule or a\nreviewer; or code, for a word match, a hook or a review check above\ntold. Promoting a told rule with nothing for code to judge opens its\nform, which asks for calls and words to match or a hook to run, and\nsaves the form and the rung together. Demoting to told keeps the form\nand stops running it. Form on any rule edits it.\n\nPUT /constraints/{id}/form sets the form and, when given, the rung; it\nrefuses checked or enforced with nothing to judge, and a charter's rule.\" && git log --oneline -3","description":"Record G3 and commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null