{"parentUuid":"6250f0fd-6ce5-4105-a31a-825e5354b4f6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgybBX5oMtj31YBstJNmR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"G3 is done: a rule can now be judged by an agent or by code, and promoting or demoting moves it between the two. It's committed as `0917c1c`. CI and the safeguard pass, and nothing is pushed.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Who judges each rule:** every constraint row now says \"agent judges it\" or \"code judges it\".\n  - An agent judges a told rule and a reviewer.\n  - Code judges a word match, a hook, or a review check, once it is above told.\n- **Promoting:** if you promote a told rule that has nothing for code to judge, an editor opens below it. It asks for calls and words to match, or a hook command. \"Save and make it enforced\" stays off until you give one, then saves the form and the rung together.\n- **Demoting:** moving a rule to told keeps its form and stops running it, so promoting it again needs no re-entry.\n- **Editing:** \"Form\" on any rule you own opens the same editor at any rung.\n- **Server:** `PUT /constraints/{id}/form` sets the form and, when given, the rung. It refuses checked or enforced with nothing to judge, and it refuses any change to a charter's rule.\n- **Grants:** they keep Ask | Allowed as their privilege axis.\n\n**Live check, at All workflows:**\n1. A told test rule showed \"agent judges it\".\n2. Enforced opened the editor. With the hook `./.agents/hooks/lint.sh` it saved as an enforced hook, and the row read \"Hook\" and \"code judges it\".\n3. Told kept the hook and stopped it running.\n4. The audit recorded the form, both promotions, and both demotions.\n\nI removed the test rule afterward.\n\nAll three phases are in now: `dbc3f40` (scopes), `d7db219` (levels) and `0917c1c` (two forms). None of them are pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":823,"cache_read_input_tokens":857780,"output_tokens":607,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":823,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":607,"cache_read_input_tokens":857780,"cache_creation_input_tokens":823,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":823},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"007da412-331e-4283-aa10-2d3c553c7491","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgybBWgVCqfBeiXoR3w3R","type":"assistant","uuid":"0497a151-0f75-46fb-b155-0e45ced462dc","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:31:29.948Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
