{"parentUuid":"f317f632-c29c-49c2-997f-ffe2e7c5bf09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgybVvD6SW47dC6KJj9yA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SToPYUe6ikvq7ZaTy51eDd","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"What is an inferential capability?","header":"Inferential cap","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Skills, agents, guidance (Recommended)","description":"Things the agent may choose to use, judged by the model: skills from .agents/skills, agents from .agents/agents, and capability notes ('you may refactor tests'). Deterministic capabilities stay the gate's grants: functions, commands, MCP tools.","preview":"CAPABILITIES\n Inferential   skill: code-review     Workspace\n               note: may edit docs    Bastion\n Deterministic sandbox::fs::read      Bastion  [Ask|Allowed]\n               mcp::github::*         Bastion  [Ask|Allowed]\n               Bash(git status)       Workspace"},{"label":"Only deterministic","description":"Capabilities are always grants the gate checks. Only constraints have an inferential side."}]},{"question":"With no rungs, what does a deterministic constraint do when a call or change breaks it?","header":"No rungs","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Always blocks (Recommended)","description":"A deterministic constraint refuses the call or sends the work back. The three seeded 'checked' review checks (assertions kept, no skip markers, tests still exist) would start blocking; I would turn them off at first so nothing changes until you turn them on.","preview":"Keep every assertion a test makes   Deterministic  Bastion  [Off]\n  (was checked: noted, never refused)"},{"label":"Block or warn","description":"A deterministic constraint has one setting: block, or warn (record it and go on). Not a rung ladder, just two behaviors."}]},{"question":"The seeded rules and grants apply to every workflow today. With the all-workflows level out of the UI, where do they show?","header":"Defaults","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"As inherited at each workflow (Recommended)","description":"They stay on for every workflow on the server. Each workflow shows them as inherited, with On/Off for that workflow and its steps. Editing them for all workflows waits until you decide that level.","preview":"Bug fix (all steps)\n Do not delete existing tests   Deterministic  Bastion\n   [Inherit · on | On | Off]"},{"label":"Copy into each workflow","description":"Each workflow gets its own copy, on at all its steps. No item applies across workflows any more."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":858603,"output_tokens":3153,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2035},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3153,"cache_read_input_tokens":858603,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SToPYUe6ikvq7ZaTy51eDd":{"questions":[{"question":"What is an inferential capability?","header":"Inferential cap","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Skills, agents, guidance (Recommended)","description":"Things the agent may choose to use, judged by the model: skills from .agents/skills, agents from .agents/agents, and capability notes ('you may refactor tests'). Deterministic capabilities stay the gate's grants: functions, commands, MCP tools.","preview":"CAPABILITIES\n Inferential   skill: code-review     Workspace\n     