{"parentUuid":"3de2d2f2-753e-4aef-a1f0-48ff7324dfe3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgybe9mdyRMagL84xUMvV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No listing exists yet, so I'm adding a list method to Machine for skills and agents, then writing the plan for the server migration and UI changes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_read_input_tokens":866859,"output_tokens":1598,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":383},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":905,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1598,"cache_read_input_tokens":866859,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":905},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b8edb6d7-ea22-4f33-b62d-90937acbd048","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgybe9R4rHitA19Hpb6HR","type":"assistant","uuid":"ff2566d4-236e-459d-bcc4-21de477a38fb","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:37:30.440Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"ff2566d4-236e-459d-bcc4-21de477a38fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgybe9mdyRMagL84xUMvV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017s6Gc1iGV6tJWoZ91tXmBn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Open questions')\nhead='''# Bastion plan: rules by who judges them\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nA step's rules sort on three questions. Is it a constraint or a\ncapability? Does an agent judge it (inferential) or code (deterministic)?\nAnd does it come from the workspace's repository or from Bastion? Each\nitem is on or off at a step, or for every step of its workflow. Told,\nchecked and enforced go: an inferential rule is said to the agent, a\ndeterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. The\ncost is the old \"checked\" rules, which noted a break and let it pass;\nthey start off, so nothing changes until you turn one on.\n\nThe scopes plan (G1 to G3) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions\nare in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 to D56.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit\nbefore the next one starts.\n\n### R1. The model on the server (D56)\n\n- A constraint's mode is inferential (stored as told) or deterministic\n  (stored as enforced). Migration 9 turns each checked one deterministic\n  and off for every workflow.\n- A constraint row may be a capability: a note told to the agent as what\n  it may do, such as a skill to use. The brief lists them under \"You may\".\n- The charter listing adds the repository's skills and agents, which a\n  workspace brings as inferential capabilities.\n- Setting a mode refuses checked.\n\n### R2. The rules view by type and mode\n\n- Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into\n  inferential and deterministic, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every\n  row.\n- A Bastion constraint has an Inferential | Deterministic switch; going\n  deterministic asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask |\n  Allowed.\n- The levels are the workflow and the step. What applies to every\n  workflow shows as inherited at the workflow; editing it for all\n  workflows waits.\n\n### R3. Docs\n\n- VISION.md and DECISIONS.md say how rules sort.\n\n'''\ns=head+s[i:]\ns=s.rstrip()+'''\n- **Rules for every workflow.** Whether some items should be set once for\n  all workflows, and where that lives.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| D55 |'); j=s.index('\\n',i)+1\ns=s[:j]+'''| D56 | A constraint or capability is inferential, which an agent judges, or deterministic, which code decides; it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: an inferential constraint is said to the agent, a deterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. An inferential capability is a skill, an agent, or a note on what the agent may do. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py PLAN.md 2>&1 | head -4","description":"Write the plan and D56"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_read_input_tokens":866859,"output_tokens":1598,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":383},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":905,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1598,"cache_read_input_tokens":866859,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":905},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017s6Gc1iGV6tJWoZ91tXmBn":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Open questions')\nhead='''# Bastion plan: rules by who judges them\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nA step's rules sort on three questions. Is it a constraint or a\ncapability? Does an agent judge it (inferential) or code (deterministic)?\nAnd does it come from the workspace's repository or from Bastion? Each\nitem is on or off at a step, or for every step of its workflow. Told,\nchecked and enforced go: an inferential rule is said to the agent, a\ndeterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. The\ncost is the old \"checked\" rules, which noted a break and let it pass;\nthey start off, so nothing changes until you turn one on.\n\nThe scopes plan (G1 to G3) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions\nare in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 to D56.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, gets a live check in the app, and lands in a commit\nbefore the next one starts.\n\n### R1. The model on the server (D56)\n\n- A constraint's mode is inferential (stored as told) or deterministic\n  (stored as enforced). Migration 9 turns each checked one deterministic\n  and off for every workflow.\n- A constraint row may be a capability: a note told to the agent as what\n  it may do, such as a skill to use. The brief lists them under \"You may\".\n- The charter listing adds the repository's skills and agents, which a\n  workspace brings as inferential capabilities.\n- Setting a mode refuses checked.\n\n### R2. The rules view by type and mode\n\n- Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into\n  inferential and deterministic, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every\n  row.\n- A Bastion constraint has an Inferential | Deterministic switch; going\n  deterministic asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask |\n  Allowed.\n- The levels are the workflow and the step. What applies to every\n  workflow shows as inherited at the workflow; editing it for all\n  workflows waits.\n\n### R3. Docs\n\n- VISION.md and DECISIONS.md say how rules sort.\n\n'''\ns=head+s[i:]\ns=s.rstrip()+'''\n- **Rules for every workflow.** Whether some items should be set once for\n  all workflows, and where that lives.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| D55 |'); j=s.index('\\n',i)+1\ns=s[:j]+'''| D56 | A constraint or capability is inferential, which an agent judges, or deterministic, which code decides; it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: an inferential constraint is said to the agent, a deterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. An inferential capability is a skill, an agent, or a note on what the agent may do. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |\n'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py PLAN.md 2>&1 | head -4","description":"Write the plan and D56"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_017s6Gc1iGV6tJWoZ91tXmBn":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b8edb6d7-ea22-4f33-b62d-90937acbd048","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgybe9R4rHitA19Hpb6HR","type":"assistant","uuid":"2380c06c-8c2c-4331-9a16-4bbc8a91cbc3","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:37:40.184Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
