eedback (stored as\n  enforced). A reviewer is feedback: it reads what the step did. Migration\n  9 turns each checked one into feedback, off for every workflow.''')\nhead=head.replace('''  workspace brings as inferential capabilities.''','''  workspace brings as feedforward capabilities.''')\nrest=s[i:]\nrest=rest.replace('''- Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into\n  inferential and deterministic, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every\n  row.\n- A Bastion constraint has an Inferential | Deterministic switch; going\n  deterministic asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask |\n  Allowed.''','''- Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into\n  feedforward and feedback, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every row.\n- A Bastion rule has a Feedforward | Feedback switch; going to feedback\n  asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask | Allowed.''')\nopen(p,'w').write(head+rest)\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('| D56 |'); j=s.index('\\n',i)\ns=s[:i]+'''| D56 | A constraint or capability is feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts (a rule it is told, a skill, an agent, a note on what it may do), or feedback, which checks what it did (a word match, a hook, a review check, a reviewer); it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: a feedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |'''+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"inferential\\|deterministic\" PLAN.md DECISIONS.md | head","description":"Rename the modes in the plan and D56"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01RgDjmir3yRjX8fvfLfLJgE":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"52d14907-8b07-4eb2-a498-44b02ba2ffb9","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgybjfpZDxnpsAf56Hf6e