{"parentUuid":"1c351675-24c3-4cad-ad0e-834809513585","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"37211818-95a6-4835-b720-c9efefd2895a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RgDjmir3yRjX8fvfLfLJgE","type":"tool_result","content":"DECISIONS.md:84:| D55 | A constraint is judged by an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or by code (a word match, a hook, a review check). Promoting a told rule gives it a deterministic form; demoting keeps the form and stops running it. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b579037f-1ee5-4538-a6ff-fcc4a4ef60dc","timestamp":"2026-11-12T19:38:56.091Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"DECISIONS.md:84:| D55 | A constraint is judged by an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or by code (a word match, a hook, a review check). Promoting a told rule gives it a deterministic form; demoting keeps the form and stops running it. |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":82,"oldLines":7,"newStart":82,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D53 | A step's rules live with the step, on the Workflows page, in one tab by layer: the charter (read-only, from the repository), the harness (grants, and the rules and hooks on calls), and the factory (review checks and reviewers). With no step picked, the page shows what applies at every step. Each rung is a switch. There is no Constraints or Capabilities page. |"," | D54 | A constraint or a grant is one item that three scopes turn on or off: all workflows (`*`), one workflow, and one step, each with `!` for off. The most specific setting wins. A list with no `*` means every step when it turns no step on, and only the steps it names otherwise. A grant is an item for one kind and one function; a step turns items on or off rather than replacing its kind's grants, which replaces D48's \"take the place of\". A rung belongs to the item, not to a scope. |"," | D55 | A constraint is judged by an agent (a told rule, a reviewer) or by code (a word match, a hook, a review check). Promoting a told rule gives it a deterministic form; demoting keeps the form and stops running it. |","-| D56 | A constraint or capability is inferential, which an agent judges, or deterministic, which code decides; it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: an inferential constraint is said to the agent, a deterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. An inferential capability is a skill, an agent, or a note on what the agent may do. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |","+| D56 | A constraint or capability is feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts (a rule it is told, a skill, an agent, a note on what it may do), or feedback, which checks what it did (a word match, a hook, a review check, a reviewer); it comes from the workspace's charter or from Bastion. Told, checked and enforced give way: a feedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. Items are on or off at a step or for every step of a workflow; the level for every workflow stays in the data but out of the app for now. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":4,"oldLines":13,"newStart":4,"newLines":14,"lines":[" <!-- voice-english: ste -->"," "," A step's rules sort on three questions. Is it a constraint or a","-capability? Does an agent judge it (inferential) or code (deterministic)?","-And does it come from the workspace's repository or from Bastion? Each","-item is on or off at a step, or for every step of its workflow. Told,","-checked and enforced go: an inferential rule is said to the agent, a","-deterministic one always blocks, and a grant keeps ask or allowed. The","-cost is the old \"checked\" rules, which noted a break and let it pass;","-they start off, so nothing changes until you turn one on.","+capability? Is it feedforward, which guides the agent before it acts, or","+feedback, which checks what it did? And does it come from the","+workspace's repository or from Bastion? Each item is on or off at a step,","+or for every step of its workflow. Told, checked and enforced go: a","+feedforward rule is said to the agent, a feedback one always blocks, and","+a grant keeps ask or allowed. The cost is the old \"checked\" rules, which","+noted a break and let it pass; they start off, so nothing changes until","+you turn one on."," "," The scopes plan (G1 to G3) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions"," are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D54 to D56."]},{"oldStart":22,"oldLines":23,"newStart":23,"newLines":21,"lines":[" "," ### R1. The model on the server (D56)"," ","-- A constraint's mode is inferential (stored as told) or deterministic","-  (stored as enforced). Migration 9 turns each checked one deterministic","-  and off for every workflow.","+- A constraint is feedforward (stored as told) or feedback (stored as","+  enforced). A reviewer is feedback: it reads what the step did. Migration","+  9 turns each checked one into feedback, off for every workflow."," - A constraint row may be a capability: a note told to the agent as what","   it may do, such as a skill to use. The brief lists them under \"You may\"."," - The charter listing adds the repository's skills and agents, which a","-  workspace brings as inferential capabilities.","+  workspace brings as feedforward capabilities."," - Setting a mode refuses checked."," "," ### R2. The rules view by type and mode"," "," - Each level shows Constraints and Capabilities, each split into","-  inferential and deterministic, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every","-  row.","-- A Bastion constraint has an Inferential | Deterministic switch; going","-  deterministic asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask |","-  Allowed.","+  feedforward and feedback, with a Workspace or Bastion chip on every row.","+- A Bastion rule has a Feedforward | Feedback switch; going to feedback","+  asks for its form, as D55 says. A grant keeps Ask | Allowed."," - The levels are the workflow and the step. What applies to every","   workflow shows as inherited at the workflow; editing it for all","   workflows waits."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"52d14907-8b07-4eb2-a498-44b02ba2ffb9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":10,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1c351675-24c3-4cad-ad0e-834809513585","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
